### Keyset paging across the seeded seven rows at two per page — FOUR pages, so "the pages all fit in
### one page" cannot be why this passes. The sort key is `priority`, which carries three deliberate
### ties (1,1 / 2,2 / 3,3): with ties the `id` tie-breaker is the only thing making the order total,
### so a boundary that lost it would repeat or skip a row and the set comparison below would catch it.
# @name Page1
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=priority.desc.nullslast
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Page2
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=priority.desc.nullslast&after={{Page1.response.body.$.next}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Page3
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=priority.desc.nullslast&after={{Page2.response.body.$.next}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Page4
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=priority.desc.nullslast&after={{Page3.response.body.$.next}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The whole set in one request, so the four pages can be compared with the truth rather than with
### each other — four pages that consistently lost the same row would agree with themselves.
# @name WholeSet
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=100&order=priority.desc.nullslast
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### A cursor no page could have issued is refused rather than answered with the first page
# @name ForgedCursor
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&after=
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `after` and `offset` anchor one window two ways, so a request carrying both is refused
# @name CursorAndOffset
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&offset=1&after={{Page1.response.body.$.next}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The other paging mode §2.1 asks for beside the keyset default
# @name OffsetPaging
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&offset=5&order=priority.desc.nullslast
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### A page size past the configured maximum is refused, never quietly clamped
# @name PageSizeTooLarge
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=5000
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
